Author: Dr. Thorsten Tepper Garcia

Created: 13 MAY 2020
Last update: 08 FEB 2021

About:

This subdirectory contains a number of patches
to files originally in pm, unless stated otherwise.

sink_particle.f90:
- added parameters
	remove_sink
	sink_tscale
	sink_tscale0
	sink_restart
to sink_params block; the first three are used in routine update_sink, the last one in routines init_sink and init_part. The first three allow to exponentially decrase the mass of a sink with time (see routine update_sink). The last one, sink_restart, if set .true., allows to include sinks at restart
via an initfile(1)/ic_sink_restart text file for a simulation that previously did not include sinks. If the simulation did include sinks, then additional sinks may be added via initfile(1)/ic_sink_restart without the need to set sink_restart

pm_parameters.f90:
- set default values for parameters
	remove_sink=.false.
	sink_tscale=1.D10
	sink_tscale0=1.D10
	sink_restart=.false.
in module pm_parameters


init_sink.f90:
- added a warnig of file 'ic_sink' or 'ic_sink_restart' not found
- added 'use pm_parameters, only: sink_restart'
- added kpc2cm, km2cm conversion factors from amr/constants.f90
- added scale_m (type real(db))
- scaled ic_sink input values to code units
- added input value 'sid' to last column
- changed slevel to levelmin in lines 258-9
- swapped lines 261 and 262:
		103  continue
     	 sinkint_level=levelmin
	to:
     	 sinkint_level=levelmin
		103  continue

	as otherwise sinkint_level remains uninitialised.
- moved output sink properties to screen to end of subroutine
- added direct force scheme information to output to screen
- added TRIM(output_dir) to filename strings where relevant


output_sink.f90:
- changed output file header string 'msink' to 'mass' for
	convenience when analysing sims with Pynbody


output_part.f90:
- split all if-clauses of the form:
  if(star.or.sink)then
	if(metal)then
	endif
  endif
into
  if(star.or.sink)then
  endif
  if(metal)then
